DESCRIPTION >
    Integrations hygiene: count of conversions with missing/zero value,
    trailing 30d. Tenant-scoped; prunes via (site_id, timestamp). Faithful 1:1
    port of api/routes/integrations.js:64-70 (queryName 'integ_missing_conv').
    Typed-column translation: properties.site_id -> site_id, event ->
    event_type.
    REAL TRANSLATION ISSUE, not a blind copy (flagged): the live condition is
    `(properties.conversion_value IS NULL OR properties.conversion_value = ''
    OR toFloatOrZero(toString(properties.conversion_value)) = 0)` — written
    for a schemaless bag value that could be absent, an empty string, or a
    non-numeric string. SCOPE_v3.md §2.6 makes `conversion_value` a typed
    `Float64 DEFAULT 0` column — explicitly NOT Nullable (it has a DEFAULT, not
    "Nullable"). Against this typed column, `IS NULL` is structurally
    impossible and `= ''` is a type mismatch (Float64 can't equal a string).
    "Missing" and "zero" collapse to the SAME stored value (0) once the column
    has a NOT-NULL default — so the faithful semantic translation is simply
    `conversion_value = 0`, not a literal copy of the three-way OR (which
    isn't even valid SQL against this column's type).
    No JSON-bag fields.
    NOT YET PUSHED — validated read-only via `tb --cloud sql` only.

NODE integ_missing_conv_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT count() AS cnt
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND event_type = '$conversion'
      AND timestamp >= now() - INTERVAL 30 DAY
      AND conversion_value = 0

TYPE endpoint
